That pairs plot looks OK --- that degree of correlation shouldn't be
a serious problem.  Are the n_eff high enough and R-hats near 1?

The varying intercepts and global fixed intercept are correlated by
design.

- Bob

> On Apr 3, 2017, at 2:26 PM, Sam Bashevkin <smbas...@ucdavis.edu> wrote:
>
> To clarify, the levels of this varying intercept are positively correlated with each other in the posterior and negatively correlated with the global intercept. The pairs plot below shows this, where ae[1:5] are the first 5 levels of my varying intercept (there are too many to display on one graph) and B[1] is my global intercept.
>

