Date: Sun, 09 Apr 2017 02:15:54 +0000
Subject: Improvements to Multidim Mixture Model Specification?
Message-ID: <_BKynyOhpKE.7hh9AeKVAAAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/_BKynyOhpKE/m/7hh9AeKVAAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Is this about as efficient as we can make a multidimensional mixture model?
There’s some additional complexity here in order to order the first component
of the means and (hopefully) identify the model.

data {
  int<lower=0> D;
  int<lower=0> K;
  int<lower = 0> N;
  vector[D] y[N];
}

transformed data {
  matrix[D, D] L = diag_matrix(rep_vector(1, D));
}

parameters {
  ordered[K] mu_head;
  vector[D - 1] mu_tail[K];
  simplex[K] lambda;
}

transformed parameters {
  vector[D] mu[K];
  for (k in 1:K) {
    mu[k, 1] = mu_head[k];
    mu[k, 2:D] = mu_tail[k];
  }
}

model {
  for (k in 1:K)
    mu[k] ~ normal(0, 5);
  lambda ~ beta(5, 5);
  for (n in 1:N) {
    vector[K] comp_lpdf;
    for (k in 1:K) {
      comp_lpdf[k] =  log(lambda[k])
                    + multi_normal_cholesky_lpdf(y[n] | mu[k], L);
    }
    target += log_sum_exp(comp_lpdf);
  }
}

