Yo Glenn, I had to do this a while ago for other reasons.

I ended up using cmdStan for my problem (on Ben Goodrich's advice). It's a little different of an interface, but it's pretty straightforward to interface C++ with it. Have a look through the manual (http://mc-stan.org/documentation/). Bonus is, if you get your stuff working with cmdStan maybe the possibility of an RStan weirdness can be totally eliminated.

It'd still be a good idea to wait on Daniel and Bob's feedback before you dive into the code, but if you wanted to get started reading, you'll want to at least read the first 13 or so sections of the Stan Math paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.07164 . That has all the nuts and bolts of how the autodiff works with lots of clean C++ examples.

Ben

