Hi Daniel,
    So this is the model I specified for the model:

"data {
    int s ;                         // Number of subjects
    int t ;                         // Number of trials per subject
    int N ;                        // total number of data points
    int resp[N] ;                  // number of total responses
    int subj[N] ;                  // Subject number
    real trial[N] ;                // Trial number
    real vot[N] ;                   //  VOT of each trial
      }

transformed data {

}

parameters {
    real a ;                         // Intercept
    real b ;                          // Slope
    real<lower = 0, upper = 0.1> lambda ;   // Lapse rate
    real k_a ;                              // Intercept change
    real k_b ;                              // Slope change
    real k_l ;                              // Lapse change
}

transformed parameters {
   real<lower = 0, upper = 1> prob[N]  ;        // Probability of choosing b for each trial
   real k_a_sum[N]   ;
   real k_b_sum[N]   ;
   real<lower = 0, upper = 0.1> k_l_sum[N]   ;

  for(i in 1: N){
   k_a_sum[i] = a  + k_a * trial[i]/t;
   k_b_sum[i] = b  +  k_b * trial[i]/t;
   k_l_sum[i] = lambda  +  k_l * trial[i]/t;
   prob[i] = (1 - k_l_sum[i]) / (1 + exp((k_a_sum[i]  - vot[i]) / k_b_sum[i])) + k_l_sum[i] * 0.5 ;
   }

}

model {

// priors
a ~  normal(20,  100)  ;
b ~  normal(0,  100)   ;
lambda ~  uniform(0, .1)   ;
k_a ~  normal(0,  1)    ;
k_b ~  normal(0,  1)   ;
k_l ~  normal(0,  .1)   ;

// model evaluation

resp ~ binomial(1, prob) ;

}

generated quantities {

real Intercept[t] ;
real Slope[t] ;
real Lapse[t] ;

for(i in 1: t){
   Intercept[i] = a  + k_a * trial[i]/t ;
   Slope[i] = b  + k_b * trial[i]/t ;
   Lapse[i] = lambda + k_l * trial[i]/t;
   }

}
"

Given how prob is specified, it should be within 0 and 1 as long as k_l_sum is larger than zero and smaller than 1. But I still sometimes get the error message I attached in my previous mail:

""Rejecting initial value:"                                                                                        " Error evaluating the log probability at the initial value."                                     "Informational Message: The current Metropolis proposal is about to be rejected because of the following issue:"
"validate transformed params: prob[k0__] is 1.38673, but must be less than or equal to 1"   "

     I got the impression that I need to change the parameterization or change the initial values. Is that where the problem is?

     And if that's what I need to do, is there any recommended principled way to do so that works best when modeling with rstan?

      Thank you so much!

Best,
Shaorong

