From u3a2c786220b0276c at groups.google.com  Sun Apr 23 15:03:14 2017
From: u3a2c786220b0276c at groups.google.com (Riccardo Fusaroli)
Date: Sun, 23 Apr 2017 15:03:14 +0000
Subject: Reproducing "Circular Inference" model in Stan - Divergent iterations issue
Message-ID: <xebvGfX7Szw.NjzIb-ELBQAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/xebvGfX7Szw/m/NjzIb-ELBQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I am currently trying to reproduce the circular inference model sketched in this paper: https://www.nature.com/articles/ncomms14218 .
When I try to fit the model I get lots of divergent iterations (and Rhat goes wild) and I could use some help in figuring out whether I'm making a trivial mistake somewhere, or as Michael Betancourt mentioned on Twitter "Your model is multimodal or has an awkward geometry and needs reparameterization". In that case, i could use some help in figuring out the best way of tacking that.

Sample Data (5 out of ca 80 participants): https://www.dropbox.com/s/g6jcj85a3w6gscg/d2.csv?dl=0

The task is a gumball task, where participants have to guess whether the next gumball extracted is red (or green). The dataset includes:
Participant Number,
ChoiceRed: whether the participant indicated the next gumball is red or not
Self: an index of how many red gumballs the participant has seen in the urn (expressed on a scale from 0 to 1)
lSelf: the logit of Self
Others: an index of how many other people the participant sees guessing red (expressed on a scale from 0 to 1)
lOthers: the logit of Others

First as a sanity check I implemented a weighted bayesian model (using the rethinking package as a crutch), which gives a few divergences, but nice traceplots and Rhats=1 on both simulated and real data. The model follows the paper previously linked, only adding the possibility for biases towards red (no matter the info) with a[Participant] and pooling information across participants.

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-5A5_61aUcjU/WPy45PvYxoI/AAAAAAAA9Is/2GOPWCWoRuUJiUyY5iuxmZULR2v2Mq2dQCLcB/s1600/Screenshot%2B2017-04-23%2B16.22.20.png>

data{
    int<lower=1> N;
    int<lower=1> N_Participant;
    int ChoiceRed[N];
    int Participant[N];
    real lSelf[N];
    real lOthers[N];
}
parameters{
    vector[N_Participant] a;
    real muA;
    vector[N_Participant] wOthers;
    real muO;
    vector[N_Participant] wSelf;
    real muS;
}
model{
    vector[N] mu;
    muS ~ normal( 0.5 , 0.1 );
    wSelf ~ normal( muS , 0.3 );
    muO ~ normal( 0.5 , 0.1 );
    wOthers ~ normal( muO , 0.3 );
    muA ~ normal( 0.5 , 0.1 );
    a ~ normal( muA , 0.1 );
    for ( i in 1:N ) {
        mu[i] = a[Participant[i]] + log((wSelf[Participant[i]] * exp(lSelf[i]) + 1 - wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1 -      wSelf[Participant[i]]) * exp(lSelf[i]) + wSelf[Participant[i]])) +      log((wOthers[Participant[i]] * exp(lOthers[i]) + 1 - wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1 -          wOthers[Participant[i]]) * exp(lOthers[i]) + wOthers[Participant[i]]));
    }
    ChoiceRed ~ binomial_logit( 1 , mu );
}
generated quantities{
    vector[N] mu;
    real dev;
    dev = 0;
    for ( i in 1:N ) {
        mu[i] = a[Participant[i]] + log((wSelf[Participant[i]] * exp(lSelf[i]) + 1 - wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1 -      wSelf[Participant[i]]) * exp(lSelf[i]) + wSelf[Participant[i]])) +      log((wOthers[Participant[i]] * exp(lOthers[i]) + 1 - wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1 -          wOthers[Participant[i]]) * exp(lOthers[i]) + wOthers[Participant[i]]));
    }
    dev = dev + (-2)*binomial_logit_lpmf( ChoiceRed | 1 , mu );
}

Next I tried to implement the circular inference model. Sorry for the ugliness of the code, I'm still figuring out how to pass functions to the model definition.

 <https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-S0G1vMo8zk8/WPy49_PtAbI/AAAAAAAA9Iw/jesN_sZrrjovQl0HvQBpLu8gd1winZTMACLcB/s1600/Screenshot%2B2017-04-23%2B16.22.35.png>

data{
    int<lower=1> N;
    int<lower=1> N_Participant;
    int ChoiceRed[N];
    int Participant[N];
    real lSelf[N];
    real lOthers[N];
}
parameters{
    vector[N_Participant] a;
    vector[N_Participant] aSelf;
    vector[N_Participant] aOthers;
    vector[N_Participant] wSelf;
    vector[N_Participant] wOthers;
    real muA;
    real muS;
    real muO;
    real<lower=0> scaleS;
    real<lower=0> scaleO;
}
model{
    vector[N] mu;
    scaleO ~ normal( 0 , 3 );
    scaleS ~ normal ( 0 , 3 );
    muO ~ normal( 0 , 1 );
    muS ~ normal( 0 , 1 );
    muA ~ normal( 0 , 1 );
    wOthers ~ normal( muO , 3 );
    wSelf ~ normal( muS , 3 );
    for ( j in 1:N_Participant ) aOthers[j] ~ cauchy( 0 , scaleO );
    for ( j in 1:N_Participant ) aSelf[j] ~ cauchy( 0 , scaleS );
    a ~ normal( muA , 3 );
    for ( i in 1:N ) {
        mu[i] = a[Participant[i]]+
    #F(lSelf + fOthers + fSelf, wSelf) +
    log((wSelf[Participant[i]]*exp(lSelf +
                                  log((wOthers[Participant[i]]*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+1-wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1-wOthers[Participant[i]])*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+wOthers[Participant[i]]))  +
                                  log((wSelf[Participant[i]]*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+1-wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1-wSelf[Participant[i]])*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+wSelf[Participant[i]])) )+
           1-wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1-wSelf[Participant[i]])*exp(lSelf +
                                                               log((wOthers[Participant[i]]*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+1-wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1-wOthers[Participant[i]])*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+wOthers[Participant[i]]))  +
                                                               log((wSelf[Participant[i]]*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+1-wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1-wSelf[Participant[i]])*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+wSelf[Participant[i]])) )+
                                    wSelf[Participant[i]])) +
    #F(lOthers + fSelf + fOthers,wOthers)
    log((wOthers[Participant[i]]*exp(lOthers +
                                    log((wSelf[Participant[i]]*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+1-wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1-wSelf[Participant[i]])*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+wSelf[Participant[i]]))  +
                                    log((wOthers[Participant[i]]*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+1-wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1-wOthers[Participant[i]])*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+wOthers[Participant[i]])) )+
           1-wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1-wOthers[Participant[i]])*exp(lOthers +
                                                                   log((wSelf[Participant[i]]*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+1-wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1-wSelf[Participant[i]])*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+wSelf[Participant[i]]))  +
                                                                   log((wOthers[Participant[i]]*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+1-wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1-wOthers[Participant[i]])*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+wOthers[Participant[i]])) )+wOthers[Participant[i]]))
    }
    ChoiceRed ~ binomial_logit( 1 , mu );
}
generated quantities{
    vector[N] mu;
    real dev;
    dev = 0;
    for ( i in 1:N ) {
        mu[i] = a[Participant[i]]+
    #F(lSelf + fOthers + fSelf, wSelf) +
    log((wSelf[Participant[i]]*exp(lSelf +
                                  log((wOthers[Participant[i]]*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+1-wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1-wOthers[Participant[i]])*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+wOthers[Participant[i]]))  +
                                  log((wSelf[Participant[i]]*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+1-wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1-wSelf[Participant[i]])*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+wSelf[Participant[i]])) )+
           1-wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1-wSelf[Participant[i]])*exp(lSelf +
                                                               log((wOthers[Participant[i]]*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+1-wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1-wOthers[Participant[i]])*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+wOthers[Participant[i]]))  +
                                                               log((wSelf[Participant[i]]*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+1-wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1-wSelf[Participant[i]])*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+wSelf[Participant[i]])) )+
                                    wSelf[Participant[i]])) +
    #F(lOthers + fSelf + fOthers,wOthers)
    log((wOthers[Participant[i]]*exp(lOthers +
                                    log((wSelf[Participant[i]]*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+1-wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1-wSelf[Participant[i]])*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+wSelf[Participant[i]]))  +
                                    log((wOthers[Participant[i]]*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+1-wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1-wOthers[Participant[i]])*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+wOthers[Participant[i]])) )+
           1-wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1-wOthers[Participant[i]])*exp(lOthers +
                                                                   log((wSelf[Participant[i]]*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+1-wSelf[Participant[i]])/((1-wSelf[Participant[i]])*exp(aSelf[Participant[i]]*lSelf)+wSelf[Participant[i]]))  +
                                                                   log((wOthers[Participant[i]]*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+1-wOthers[Participant[i]])/((1-wOthers[Participant[i]])*exp(aOthers[Participant[i]]*lOthers)+wOthers[Participant[i]])) )+wOthers[Participant[i]]))
    }
    dev = dev + (-2)*binomial_logit_lpmf( ChoiceRed | 1 , mu );
}

Many thanks for the attention.

