The most likely failure here looks to me to be the
constraint you put on k_l_sum --- given that it's defined
to have lower=0 and upper=0.1 and has a term that is
unconstrained, you aren't going to have much luck initializing.
You want to make sure that everything is well defined for
every set of parameters that satisfy the declared constraints.

As Daniel says, putting print() [or reject()] statements in will let
you verify where things are going wrong.

You can speed this up a lot by bracketing (trial[i] / t) because otherwise
arithmetic is left associative and you incur a couple autodiff operations
multiplying parameters by constraints --- even better save trial[i] / t
in transformed parameters.

- Bob

