On Wednesday, April 19, 2017 at 1:11:21 PM UTC-4, Dalton Hance wrote:
> But for simplicity lets imagine that no fish die, all fish migrate downstream, and detection at station 4 (the last station) is perfect.

If you are going to assume all that I would model the time to station 1, 2, and 3 as some proportion of the time to station 4.  Conceptually, you have a fish-specific simplex, but for some fish, the proportion of time to station 1, 2, and 3 is observed. So, then you have beta or Dirichlet variates as proportions between any two observed points. You can use the stick-breaking construction in the Stan User Manual.

Ben

