If you search "c++ exception (unknown reason)" in stan-user mail list, actually you would find this is not the first time this type of error happens to just some users.  And we never figure out why.

If you have an error like this, please run the follow code and provide your results.

library(inline)
library(Rcpp)

sessionInfo()

cppcode <- "
  int i = Rcpp::as<int>(x);
  if (i > 0) throw std::invalid_argument(\"invalid arg error.\");
  else if (i < 0) throw i;
  return R_NilValue;
"

inccode <- "#include <Rcpp.h>"

foo <- cxxfunction(signature(x='integer'), inc=inccode, body=cppcode, plugin='Rcpp', verbose=TRUE)

foo(1L)

# this throws "c++ exception (unknown reason)"
foo(-2L)

foo(0L)

