Hi Stephano,

I'm not really sure what you mean. I looked at the original post and I'm not following. Can you write a Stan function to compute it? Maybe that would help.

In Stan, matrices have 2 (and only 2) dimensions. Arrays can have as many dimensions as you want. And you can have arrays of any type.

Regarding speed, I'd first think about having a working implementation before even considering how fast it goes.

Daniel

